The extension runs only on audible.com pages (host match *://*.audible.com/*)
and requests no permissions. It makes no network requests and transmits no
data. The only thing stored is the on/off state of the "Exclude AI-narrated
titles" checkbox on Audible's advanced search page, kept in audible.com's own
localStorage in your browser. When that checkbox is on, the term
-virtual_voice is added to the search keywords you submit to Audible.
